[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4825618784","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120673#issuecomment-4825618784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120673","id":4825618784,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABH6EZYA","user":{"login":"jvron","id":205451073,"node_id":"U_kgDODD7vQQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/205451073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron","html_url":"https://github.com/jvron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-28T09:50:12Z","updated_at":"2026-06-28T09:50:12Z","body":"I investigated this issue and found the problem appears to be missing boolean to float/uint/int conversion handling during built-in constructor validation. While testing, I also found that constant conversion did not support boolean-to-float/uint/int conversions.\n\nWith a local fix, the following now compile correctly:\n\nvec2(false);\nvec3(false);\nvec4(false);\n\nivec2(false);\nivec3(false);\nivec4(false);\n\nuvec2(false);\nuvec3(false);\nuvec4(false);\n\nI'm testing for regressions and will open a PR if everything looks good.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4825618784/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4826681809","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120673#issuecomment-4826681809","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120673","id":4826681809,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABH7FR0Q","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-28T16:19:50Z","updated_at":"2026-06-28T16:19:50Z","body":"```\nvec3 v = vec3(false); <-- won't compile\nvec3 v = vec3(float(false)); <-- works as expected\n```\nImo this is not a bug, this should be the behaviour. Trying to create a `vec3` from a `bool` should be a bug in 99% of cases, and when you want to do it deliberately, you can cast.\n\nWhy do you think this is a bug?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4826681809/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4828981971","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120673#issuecomment-4828981971","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120673","id":4828981971,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABH9Rq0w","user":{"login":"ahs3n","id":68795918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4Nzk1OTE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68795918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n","html_url":"https://github.com/ahs3n","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-29T04:23:16Z","updated_at":"2026-06-29T05:03:49Z","body":"imo it is a bug because it is a significant difference from expected glsl behaviour and would prevent copying glsl directly to gdshader for no beneficial reason. Since the language is strictly typed, there's not really any way you can do this by accident either. C++ converts bool to int and vice versa implicitly as well. \n\nI write a lot of glsl, and discovered this discrepancy my first day writing shaders in Godot so I'd say it's worth fixing. It's quite useful for quickly testing conditions, and I have never experienced a bug from this behaviour.\n\nI may be biased because for me, glsl is almost the perfect language, and gdshader subtly improves on its limitations. It would be a tremendous shame for it to lose any functionality.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4828981971/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4829849792","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120673#issuecomment-4829849792","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120673","id":4829849792,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABH-GowA","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:06:36Z","updated_at":"2026-06-29T07:06:36Z","body":"I guess if glsl does this natively, that is a decent argument to supporting them I guess (although I personally prefer explicit).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4829849792/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4920095769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120673#issuecomment-4920095769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120673","id":4920095769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJUK0GQ","user":{"login":"ahs3n","id":68795918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4Nzk1OTE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68795918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n","html_url":"https://github.com/ahs3n","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahs3n/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T23:29:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T23:29:37Z","body":"There's also an argument to be made that `vec3(true)` actually _is_ explicit because a `vecN` is always float and only float. There's `ivecN` and `bvecN` for integers and booleans respectively","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4920095769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]